    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a `title`/`salutation` feature to the `POST`/`GET /api/owners` flow, placing each piece where it belongs:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (source of the generated DTOs):\n   - Added `title` to the `OwnerFields` schema \u2014 an optional request input constrained by pattern `^(MR|MRS|MS|DR)$` (kept as a plain `String`, not an enum, so it maps entity\u2194DTO without custom converters).\n   - Added `salutation` as a `readOnly` string on the `Owner` response schema.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a persisted `title` column with getter/setter, so a title supplied at create time survives to the `GET`.\n\n3. **Schema DDL** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added a single-responsibility `salutation(Owner)` default method (`title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title) wired via `@Mapping`, sitting alongside the existing derived-field methods like `displayName`. MapStruct maps the plain `title` field automatically in both directions, so no pipeline function was needed.\n\nThe `coreComposesSalutation` acceptance test (`title=DR`, `lastName=who` \u2192 `salutation=DR who`) and the rest of the suite are green.",
